{
  "id": "P064",
  "slug": "ipv4-validator",
  "title": "Strict IPv4 Address Validator",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "tags": [
    "strings",
    "parsing"
  ],
  "estimatedMinutes": 12,
  "relatedModules": [
    "a3-strings-io",
    "a4-control-flow"
  ],
  "entry": {
    "type": "function",
    "name": "is_valid_ipv4"
  },
  "compare": "exact",
  "tests": {
    "visible": [
      {
        "label": "Valid loopback and gateway IP",
        "args": [
          "192.168.0.1"
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "label": "Leading zero octet rejected cleanly",
        "args": [
          "192.168.01.1"
        ],
        "expected": false
      }
    ],
    "hidden": [
      {
        "label": "All zeros valid",
        "args": [
          "0.0.0.0"
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "label": "Max octets 255 valid",
        "args": [
          "255.255.255.255"
        ],
        "expected": true
      },
      {
        "label": "Out of range octet 256 rejected",
        "args": [
          "256.1.1.1"
        ],
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "label": "Sign or space inside octet rejected",
        "args": [
          "+1.2.3.4"
        ],
        "expected": false
      },
      {
        "label": "Double zero octet \"00\" rejected",
        "args": [
          "10.00.0.1"
        ],
        "expected": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "hints": [
    "Split on \".\" and require len(parts) == 4.",
    "For each part: check `part.isdigit()` (and `all(\"0\" <= ch <= \"9\" ...)` so non-ASCII Unicode digits fail too), `len(part) == 1 or not part.startswith(\"0\")`, and `0 <= int(part) <= 255`.",
    "Pseudocode:\n  parts = ip.split(\".\")\n  if len(parts) != 4: return False\n  for p in parts:\n      if not p or not all(\"0\" <= c <= \"9\" for c in p): return False\n      if len(p) > 1 and p[0] == \"0\": return False\n      if int(p) > 255: return False\n  return True"
  ],
  "sources": [
    "python-tutorial",
    "python-stdtypes-docs"
  ]
}
